# Distinction and Relation

This file defines the first move after undifferentiated symmetry.

The first move is not an object.

The first move is not a particle.

The first move is not a location.

The first move is not a clock-tick.

Those are too late.

The first move must be more basic.

The current candidate is:

**distinction / relation**

## Why distinction

Undifferentiated symmetry means maximal sameness before difference.

So the first break cannot begin with a finished thing.

A finished thing already requires a boundary.

A boundary already requires distinction.

So before there can be an object, there must be a difference.

The first move is:

this / not-this

Not yet as objects.

Not yet as places.

Not yet as particles.

Only as distinction.

## Why relation

A distinction is never one-sided.

To distinguish is already to relate.

If there is this, there is not-this.

If there is a marked side, there is an unmarked side.

If there is a boundary, there is what the boundary separates.

So distinction and relation may not be two separate events.

They may be the same first event seen from two sides.

Distinction gives difference.

Relation gives the difference structure.

## The first two-sidedness

The first distinction creates two-sidedness:

this / not-this  
marked / unmarked  
inside / outside potential  
same / not-same  
held / not-held  

This is not yet ordinary space.

This is not yet ordinary time.

This is not yet a physical object.

It is the first condition under which any later object, space, time, or measure could become meaningful.

## Why this matters

If the model begins with an object, it has already assumed distinction.

If the model begins with a location, it has already assumed relation.

If the model begins with motion, it has already assumed time and difference.

So this repo moves earlier.

Before object, there is distinction.

Before location, there is relation.

Before motion, there is difference that can be compared.

## Relation before locality

Locality means things can be placed as here or there.

But here and there require a frame.

At this stage, there is not yet a frame.

So relation comes before locality.

Relation does not yet mean distance.

It means structured difference.

Distance may come later.

Location may come later.

Locality may come later.

But relation is required first.

## Distinction is not yet measure

Distinction gives difference.

It does not yet give amount.

It can say:

this is not that

But it cannot yet say:

how far  
how long  
how much  
how curved  
how dense  

So distinction is not the ruler.

It is only the first break that may make a ruler possible later.

## Current claim

The first move after undifferentiated symmetry is distinction / relation.

A distinction is automatically relational.

A relation is automatically structured by distinction.

So the first event may be:

difference becoming two-sided.

## Current edge

Distinction gives the first break.

Relation gives the first structure.

But one distinction is not yet a world.

The next question is:

Can distinction repeat?

Can the first difference return into itself?

Can distinction distinguish distinction?

That next move is:

**re-entry**
